  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Cgi Federal obligated $1.1B in FY2026 to date across 257 awards, with an average award size of $4.1M. Obligations fell 10.9% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a steady band: FY21 $1B, FY22 $1.1B, FY23 $1.1B, FY24 $1.2B, FY25 $1.2B, FY26 $1.1B. The Department of State is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date at $221M, followed by the General Services Administration at $172M and the Department of Justice at $138M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $136M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $76M. Other Computer Related Services is Cgi Federal's largest market at $440M, with Computer Systems Design Services at $212M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $193M. Facilities Support Services, Computing Infrastructure Providers, and Research and Development (physical, engineering, life sciences) round out the higher-value markets with $66M, $54.1M, and $50.6M respectively. This profile reflects where obligations concentrate and which agencies and NAICS markets account for most federal activity this fiscal year to date.",
